---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/home/Masthead.astro';
import AboutPhoto from '../components/about/AboutPhoto.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';

const photos = {
	hero: '/images/about/devconf-speaking.jpg',
	uxpa: '/images/about/uxpa-community.jpg',
	family: '/images/about/family-moment.jpg',
	team: '/images/about/team-celebration.jpg',
};
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About me"
	description="Kevin Hatchoua on design, public service, open source, and community."
	hideSiteHeader
>
	<Masthead active="about" />

	<article class="about-page">
		<header class="about-hero mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 pb-16 pt-10 md:px-8 md:pb-24 md:pt-14">
			<div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-14">
				<div class="lg:col-span-5" data-reveal>
					<AboutPhoto
						src={photos.hero}
						alt="Kevin Hatchoua speaking at DevConf, applauding at a conference podium"
						caption="Sharing ideas in the open at DevConf."
						aspect="portrait"
						objectPosition="center 22%"
						variant="hero"
					/>
				</div>
				<div class="lg:col-span-7" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
					<p class="font-sans text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-md-primary">
						About me
					</p>
					<h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-md-on-surface md:text-5xl">
						Community, craft, and design that stays human.
					</h1>
					<p class="mt-6 font-sans text-lg leading-relaxed text-md-on-surface-variant">
						I am Kevin Hatchoua, a catalyst for change and Senior User Experience Designer at Red Hat.
						Since moving to the United States from Cameroon as a child, I have been fueled by a simple
						commitment: empower children, expand opportunity, and narrow disparities between
						communities.
					</p>
					<p class="mt-4 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-md-on-surface-variant">
						Today I shape discover, learn, try, and onboarding journeys across the open hybrid cloud,
						contribute to the PatternFly design system, and support inclusion through Red Hat
						B.U.I.L.D. Off the clock you will find me mentoring through BU Spark!, volunteering with
						UXPA Boston, and serving on the boards of Virtual Activism and AfriHope.
					</p>
					<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
						<Button href="/contact">Get in touch</Button>
						<Button href="/" variant="ghost">View projects</Button>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</header>

		<section class="about-chapter border-t border-md-outline-variant/50 bg-md-surface-container-low">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
					<div data-reveal>
						<h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-md-on-surface">Open collaboration at Red Hat</h2>
						<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 font-sans text-md-on-surface-variant">
							<p>
								My Red Hat team is where open collaboration is everyday practice: designers, engineers,
								product managers, and docs partners working in the open, sharing work early, and
								improving it together. We succeed when feedback is welcome, assumptions are tested, and
								everyone can contribute regardless of role or tenure.
							</p>
							<p>
								Inclusivity and resiliency are how we sustain that pace. I help create rooms where people
								can bring their full perspective, recover quickly when plans shift, and keep hybrid cloud
								experiences coherent for customers who depend on us. That mindset carries into
								PatternFly, B.U.I.L.D., and the cross-functional programs that shape how Red Hat shows up
								for users.
							</p>
						</div>
						<p class="mt-6">
							<a
								href="https://design.redhat.com/designer-stories/kevin-hatchoua.html"
								class="font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-md-primary no-underline hover:text-md-primary-hover"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer"
							>
								Red Hat Design designer story →
							</a>
						</p>
					</div>
					<AboutPhoto
						src={photos.team}
						alt="Kevin Hatchoua with his Red Hat team at a celebration"
						caption="My Red Hat team: building in the open and celebrating milestones together."
						objectPosition="center 35%"
						variant="story"
					/>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-chapter">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
					<AboutPhoto
						src={photos.uxpa}
						alt="Kevin Hatchoua volunteering at a UXPA Boston elections event"
						caption="Volunteering Chair, UXPA Boston board."
						objectPosition="center 20%"
						variant="accent"
						class="lg:order-1"
					/>
					<div class="lg:order-2" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
						<h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-md-on-surface">Community in practice</h2>
						<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 font-sans text-md-on-surface-variant">
							<p>
								As Volunteering Chair on the UXPA Boston board, I help New England's largest UX chapter
								stay welcoming for emerging designers and sustainable for volunteers. Conference
								programming, mentorship, and blind-reviewed speaker pipelines are how we lower barriers
								and keep the craft generous.
							</p>
							<p>
								My UXPA bio mirrors what I believe on every project: design and technology only matter
								when they create real community impact. That is why nonprofit board service with Virtual
								Activism and AfriHope stays central to how I work, not an aside on a resume.
							</p>
						</div>
						<p class="mt-6">
							<a
								href="https://uxpaboston.org/board/kevin-hatchoua/"
								class="font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-md-primary no-underline hover:text-md-primary-hover"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer"
							>
								UXPA Boston board profile →
							</a>
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-chapter border-t border-md-outline-variant/50 bg-md-surface-container-low">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
				<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center" data-reveal>
					<h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-md-on-surface">Mentorship at BU Spark!</h2>
					<p class="mt-6 font-sans text-lg leading-relaxed text-md-on-surface-variant">
						Through Boston University's Spark! Experts in Residence program, I mentor CDS student teams on
						human-centered computing: problem framing, research synthesis, prototype storytelling, and
						stakeholder reviews that respect semester timelines. Spark! is where industry craft meets
						student ambition, and where I get to pay forward the mentors who shaped me.
					</p>
					<p class="mt-6">
						<a
							href="https://www.bu.edu/spark/about/eirs/"
							class="font-sans text-sm font-semibold text-md-primary no-underline hover:text-md-primary-hover"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							BU Spark! Experts in Residence →
						</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-chapter">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-end gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
					<div class="lg:col-span-7" data-reveal>
						<h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-md-on-surface">Life away from the canvas</h2>
						<p class="mt-6 font-sans text-lg leading-relaxed text-md-on-surface-variant">
							The best ideas arrive when I am present with family: silly faces on a sunny day, long walks,
							and reminders that the work is always in service of real people. I bring that same warmth
							into facilitation, critique, and the rooms where decisions get made.
						</p>
						<p class="mt-6 font-sans text-md-on-surface-variant">
							For the fuller professional timeline, including Red Hat, Mass.gov, and open source
							contributions, see my
							<a
								href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kevinhatchoua/"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer"
								class="font-semibold text-md-primary"
							>
								LinkedIn profile</a
							>.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="lg:col-span-5" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
						<AboutPhoto
							src={photos.family}
							alt="Kevin Hatchoua with family outdoors on a bright day"
							caption="Joy keeps the work honest."
							aspect="square"
							objectPosition="center 40%"
							variant="story"
						/>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
